{
  "commit": "a89dfcd61659042841da7aa12c238ac89e4aa739",
  "instructions": "Physical role: Display & Video Sink. Controls LG webOS TVs. Connects downstream of the AVR (Onkyo) or switches video inputs directly; delegates master volume control to the AVR when volume_owner is 'external'. Call webos_get_status first: it says whether each TV is on, what is in front, and (capabilities, limitations) what works on it. With several TVs, name one with `tv`; a call without it is refused rather than guessed. When a TV's sound goes to a receiver (volume_owner 'external'), volume belongs to the receiver's own server (onkyo_set_volume), not to this one. A TV that is off doesn't answer: power 'off' means off or off the network, and webos_set_power on wakes it. To type, prefer webos_insert_text over walking an on-screen keyboard with webos_send_key, where get_status lists text_input; it only reaches system text fields (LG's search), so for YouTube use webos_search_app.",
  "package": "webos_mcp",
  "server": "webos",
  "tools": [
