      "description": "Type text into the TV's focused text field, instead of walking an on-screen keyboard with keys.\n\n<use_case>\nFill a search box or other text field on the TV in one call: e.g. open LG's search and type\n\"lofi beats\", then webos_submit_text.\n</use_case>\n\n<important_notes>\n- Only works where get_status lists `text_input`, and only in *system* text fields (LG's own\n  search, and fields that use the TV's keyboard). The field must already have focus.\n- Refused, with nothing sent, when no system field has focus. YouTube and Netflix draw their\n  own keyboards and never have one: use `webos_search_app` for YouTube, or `webos_send_key`\n  (arrows, ENTER) on the app's keyboard.\n- Confirmed by the field's reported length where the TV reports it; a warning says when not.\n</important_notes>\n",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "replace": {
            "default": false,
            "description": "True: replace everything in the field. False: add at the cursor.",
            "title": "Replace",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "text": {
            "description": "What to type: one line, up to 200 characters (no newlines; submit with webos_submit_text).",
            "maxLength": 200,
            "minLength": 1,
            "title": "Text",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "tv": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "description": "Which TV: its name (e.g. a room), an alias, or its address. Omit when there is only one; with several, a call without it is refused rather than guessed.",
            "title": "Tv"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "text"
        ],
        "title": "webos_insert_textArguments",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "webos_insert_text",
      "outputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "detail": {
            "title": "Detail",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "outcome": {
            "enum": [
